Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(-2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =-2T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}7 \\ 9\end{aligned}] & =-2T({v}_{1})+[\begin{aligned}-3 \\ 5\end{aligned}] \\ -2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}7 \\ 9\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}-3 \\ 5\end{aligned}] \\ -2T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}10 \\ 4\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =\frac{1}{-2}[\begin{aligned}10 \\ 4\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-5 \\ -2\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$
